[#:seon.task{:name "a-dig-form-through-a-list-index-reads-nil",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "A cut under a list or seq member prints a continuation through plain get-in, e.g. (subs (get-in result/e… [0]) 127) for (\"long string\"): get-in does not index a list or seq, so the offered dig form reads nil and subs throws. `seon.print/continuation` chooses get-in from the path alone; the value printer's member step for a non-vector sequential is a plain index. Done when every printed continuation, evaluated on the held value, returns the cut's rest (a regression evaluating the continuation form for list, lazy-seq and vector members).",
            :must-read
            #{seon.print/continuation seon.render.value/admit-member},
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/source-display/review-printer-opus-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "multiline-literals-hide-line-breaks-from-layout",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "7619b8dfd string-literal emits physical newlines inside one :text op. fipp.engine annotate-rights and format-nodes count all text characters as one column span, so following groups do not know the final line column. Original lane reports a long line after a multiline string overflowing width. Preserve exact string content (including blank/trailing lines); use dependency layout semantics without adding indentation inside literal contents. Distinguish inherently unbreakable long source lines from layout-added overflow; add nested map/vector regressions.",
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/source-display/review-printer-codex-notes.md"}}

 #:seon.task{:name "elision-forms-call-a-seon-helper"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A cut under a set member or a non-keyword map key prints (drop 32 (`seon.print/value-at` result/e092ae498f621 '[[:seon.render.data/entry 0 :seon.render.data/val]])) (default 2026-10-08), where clojure.core says (drop 32 (val (nth (seq result/e092ae498f621) 0))). Owner ruling 2026-10-08: elision forms use only clojure.core on the live result symbol. Done when every offered elision form names only clojure.core functions and the result symbol (nth, seq, key, val for typed steps), asserted on the form's symbols and its value through the MCP entrance."
             :must-read #{seon.print/continuation seon.print/value-at}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/printer-rules/printer-rules-opus-printer-rules.md"}}

 #:seon.task{:name "the-printer-law-lint-refuses-nothing"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "The one-printer rule is a clj-kondo :discouraged-var warning (.clj-kondo/config.edn), and bin/lane commit and the edit hook refuse only errors, so 183 printer findings landed and nothing refuses the next; bin/seon-hook (21 pr-str) is never linted; with-out-str, print bindings, Throwable->map, hand-built elision text and value-printing error messages are not detected. Done when a :seon/printer-law linter at :error, with a per-file ratchet baseline, refuses a candidate that adds (pr-str x), a hand-built N more text or (binding [*print-length* 5] …) outside seon.print, seon.render.value, seon.sci.admit and seon.id."
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/printer-rules/printer-rules-opus-printer-rules.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-member-cut-costs-more-than-it-hides"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(zipmap (range 2000) (map #(hash-map :id % :name (str \"item-\" %) :tags #{:a :b}) (range 2000))) showed 1,388 tokens of which about 810 are 29 per-entry cuts, each a 28-token dig form hiding one 4-token :tags member (default 2026-10-08). Nothing keeps a member whole when its printed size is under its continuation's. Done when no cut is emitted for a member smaller than its dig form and a regression bounds the zipmap reply. Same producer as seon.print/elision-forms-call-a-seon-helper."
             :must-read #{seon.print/continuation}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/agent-messages/messages-opus-messages.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-display-budget-override-is-not-installed"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`(binding [seon.print/*budget* 4000] (vec (range 3000)))` in an agent's SCI context answers \"Unable to resolve var: seon.print/*budget*\" (default 32ca5f2e5, agent reply-census, 2026-10-08), so the owner-ruled override (PR-11) does not exist and nothing can widen one form past the 1,500-token profile budget. Done when the same form prints up to 4,000 tokens with one finding naming the override's token count, and the same form past the model ceiling is capped with a finding."
             :must-read #{seon.render.value/render-ai-data seon.print/continuation}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/reply-census/reply-census.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-child-cap-starves-small-elements"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`(vec (repeat 400 {:a 1 :b \"two\" :c [1 2 3]}))` shows 311 tokens of the 1,500-token budget because `:seon.render.profile/max-children` (32) cuts the vector at 32 members while 1,189 tokens are unspent (default 2026-10-08), while the 2,000-entry map spends 1,388 tokens on 32 fat entries: the child count, not the token budget, decides what a collection shows. Done when members are admitted until the profile's token budget is spent (the count cap only a backstop) and a regression shows 400 small maps filling the budget, each cut naming its count and a clojure.core continuation."
             :must-read #{seon.render.value/render-ai-data}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/reply-census/reply-census.md"}}
#:seon.task{:name "stored-or-compared-text-printed-under-ambient-bindings"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.fn` stored a contract's text with plain `pr-str`, so publication (namespace maps on) and an agent evaluation (off) stored different text and digests for the same contract, and `*print-length*` made `seon.schema/canonical-definition` refuse every contract (fixed for those owners in e5cfb80dc with `seon.id/printed`). Census every `pr-str`/`prn-str`/`print-str` whose output is stored, hashed, compared or sorted in src/ and convert each to data comparison or `seon.id/printed` (AGENTS.md: one printer; identity is a structural digest, never printed text; ledger PR-24, PR-17)."
             :must-read #{seon.id/printed}}]
